  "executive_briefing": "In 2026, the international tax architecture continues its profound structural transformation, dominated by the active operationalization of the OECD's Pillar Two 15% global minimum tax. With over 60 to 140 inclusive framework jurisdictions implementing GloBE and top-up rules, multinational enterprises face complex compliance landscapes alongside newly released OECD corporate tax statistics. Simultaneously, regional hubs across ASEAN and Singapore are calibrating local corporate income tax frameworks, offering tailored cash rebates and grants to protect foreign direct investment. Concurrently, international trade continues to face intense friction driven by active tariff disputes, emergency power legal challenges, and a rapid worldwide acceleration toward mandatory e-invoicing and real-time transaction controls.",
